# __REPO_NAME__ — your training repo

This is **your** repo for working through your training curriculum. Each session is an
interactive conversation with your trainer's assistance; the repo handles git, session
branches, and PRs for you automatically. This README is your operating manual — how to
run **this** repo. You never need to know how it was built.

## Where everything goes

All your work lives under **`__TRAINEE__/`**:

| Folder | What goes here |
|---|---|
| `__TRAINEE__/sourceDocs/` | Source & reference material (add anything external here **before** using it) |
| `__TRAINEE__/inputDocs/` | Documents **you** write during a session |
| `__TRAINEE__/outputDocs/` | Summaries & documents the assistant produces for you |
| `__TRAINEE__/sessions/` | Per-session working notes (`__TRAINEE___{date}_session-N/`) |
| `__TRAINEE__/trainee-profile.md` | Who you are + what you want from the course (anchors every example) |
| `__TRAINEE__/training-state.md` | Where you are in the curriculum |
| `__TRAINEE__/feedback.md` · `improvement-recommendations.md` | Your trainer's running notes |

Nothing you produce should land at the repo **root** — always inside `__TRAINEE__/`.

## Starting a session

1. Clone your repo and run `claude`.
2. Paste a first message whose **first line** is your brief id:

   ```text
   Brief: training/{date}-{curriculum-slug}-{your-handle}
   Hi! Continue with my brief. If it's FULLY complete, include a line
   `Brief-Status: complete` in your final response; otherwise it stays in progress for
   my next session. If I'm blocked, raise it to my trainer and exit.
   ```

That is the whole launch ritual — **no git, no environment variables.** The brief must
already be **approved** by your trainer (they author it once per curriculum); if it
isn't, the session will stop and tell you — that's not an error, just ask your trainer.

## What happens automatically

- **At session start** you are moved onto a fresh session branch off `main`.
- **While you work**, if you try to read a document from **outside** this repo you'll
  get a reminder to copy it into `__TRAINEE__/sourceDocs/` first (keeps your context
  contained and reproducible).
- **At session end** (a clean exit) the assistant writes your session summary, copies
  the session log into `logs/`, commits your work, pushes the branch, and opens a
  **pull request to `main`**.

## The next-session ritual

Your **next** session starts by reviewing the PR your last session opened: read the
summary, check the work, and **merge** it. Then paste the same `Brief:` line to
continue where you left off. Many sessions accumulate on one brief — that's your
progress over time.

## First time on this workstation?

The repo needs a little one-time setup before a brief will load (a Qdrant key, `gh`
auth). Work through **`docs/workstation-setup.md`** with your trainer, then run
`python3 .claude/hooks/trainee-preflight.py` to confirm everything is ready. The full
list is in `docs/dependency-analysis.md`. Until then the repo stays quiet — you can
still read everything here.
